Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "The head of the resulting expression is the symbol ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["TensorNetwork",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/TensorNetwork"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"a89404d4-34f1-44b0-ac92-d6083a61e5b9"],
 " itself. The paclet installs a custom summary box, so the object renders as \
a single compact glyph in the front end rather than unfolding into a \
screen-filling list of numeric entries. This matters when you start composing \
operations \[LongDash] the object can be passed around, stored, and combined \
without ever spilling its tensor data into the output history."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"28c7870b-26cb-4da6-871b-df1f6bb66a34"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Head", "[", "tn", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[5]:=",ExpressionUUID->"742c4d2e-5097-4519-95c9-80f4d5d3f90b"],

Cell[BoxData["TensorNetwork"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.988058778461569*^9, 3.9880650945981283`*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[5]=",
 CellID->1214002428,ExpressionUUID->"ca57f585-ebda-45c8-8909-a37f1e4adf36"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "Use ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["TensorNetworkQ",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/TensorNetworkQ"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"6973dcb1-c814-4cea-a25a-788db420bd91"],
 " to test whether an expression is a valid network. It checks both the head \
and the structural invariants (lengths agree, every hyperedge length equals \
the rank of its tensor, every output leg is a label that actually appears). \
Predicates of this form are useful as guards inside ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["PatternTest",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/PatternTest"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"b432653c-d662-46a6-b180-dd64bccab017"],
 " constructions."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7145166b-7de3-4a6d-b93d-652b8c5089af"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"TensorNetworkQ", "[", "tn", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[6]:=",ExpressionUUID->"06e5ae0e-4045-4cb7-8950-ade1e938d48d"],

Cell[BoxData["True"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9880587805630217`*^9, 3.988065094612356*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[6]=",
 CellID->496677249,ExpressionUUID->"8af4cfe0-6838-4727-a25e-f633fd8567d3"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "The free indices are the ones that appear in exactly one hyperedge \
\[LongDash] the network's open legs. When the output specification is ",
 StyleBox["Automatic", "Code"],
 ", the free-index list is computed automatically by counting label \
occurrences. The next section shows how to override that to expose contracted \
legs or to scalar-out."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0638d88e-40f1-4c90-8c78-3a43269b1c72"],

