Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["2.6. Output permutation via Cycles", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"aa1153d6-65ce-42b2-ad6f-ab64b8041876"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "The third argument of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["TensorNetwork",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/TensorNetwork"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"a1f7eeeb-b93f-45ed-a6eb-eecb7cb82232"],
 " accepts either an explicit list of free indices, or a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Cycles",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:ref/Cycles"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "e5a79882-cf73-4b96-a6a6-2ed393886279"],
 " permutation that is applied to the auto-derived free-index order. The ",
 StyleBox["Cycles", "Code"],
 " form is convenient when you want to keep the default selection of free \
indices but reorder them \[LongDash] for instance, when downstream code \
expects rows before columns rather than the order in which they happened to \
appear in the hyperedge list."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"70f97eb0-c826-4e06-b2dd-b68f1102873a"],

