Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "The arrow notation ",
 StyleBox["1 -> 2", "Code"],
 " in the new hyperedge list denotes the rewritten leg name: it reads as \
\"the copy of the old index 2 that hangs off tensor 1.\" Each original tensor \
keeps one of these distinguished names instead of the shared label, and the \
new delta tensor connects them all. The naming is a record of where the \
spider came from."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2c366b73-20cc-4c38-84c9-9f01267b6a71"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"bin", "[", "\"\<Hyperedges\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[65]:=",ExpressionUUID->"d026ba28-27f3-47ce-9970-0825e6f06029"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", 
     RowBox[{"1", "\[Rule]", "2"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"2", "\[Rule]", "2"}], ",", "3"}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"3", "\[Rule]", "2"}], ",", "4"}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"1", "\[Rule]", "2"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"2", "\[Rule]", "2"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"3", "\[Rule]", "2"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.988059700340703*^9, 3.988065096429495*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[65]=",
 CellID->144561414,ExpressionUUID->"93761877-af99-40e9-aa21-c831cb4ab616"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "High-level contraction code applies this transformation automatically \
\[LongDash] ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["OptimalContractionPath",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/OptimalContractionPath"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"83b86e49-4fb7-44b0-b90d-4f6ed0a6b2fa"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["TensorNetworkContract",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/TensorNetworkContract"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"a7f03a76-bc40-48ce-9bfb-e5c6697444c0"],
 " both call ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["BinaryTensorNetwork",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/BinaryTensorNetwork"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"6fd22c6d-10ba-4779-a441-66864747351a"],
 " internally on non-binary input, so you rarely need to invoke it directly. \
Knowing what it does, however, makes the resulting paths legible: every \
spider in the output trace is one of these inserted vertices, not a tensor \
from the original network."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9f340664-f414-447a-b4e3-ece8d8f0ef22"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["6. Edits and transformations", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"3f12f097-e927-4485-8a35-5bdd1dd35d90"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Networks are immutable values: transformations return new networks rather \
than mutating in place. The paclet exposes a small set of structural edits \
\[LongDash] adding and deleting tensors, renaming indices \[LongDash] plus \
one bulk storage conversion to sparse representation, and one accessor that \
returns the network in its annotated-graph form for use with the full ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Graph",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/Graph"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"9392d145-aeab-45b7-9421-7736a52e3801"],
 " API. The edits compose freely: every transformation accepts a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["TensorNetwork",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/TensorNetwork"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"894e7fbc-e219-48b9-af6c-f38fa59def6c"],
 " and produces a fresh ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["TensorNetwork",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/TensorNetwork"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"b6fda57c-e705-4975-825c-8afe04346915"],
 " (or, where noted, a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Graph",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/Graph"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"de198cb9-b28f-4b34-bcf4-045a8479b6b6"],
 " form), so longer-running pipelines can be built by chaining them with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["ReplaceAll",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/ReplaceAll"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"e1da8537-5867-49c3-8351-8abf755ba897"],
 " or ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["Composition",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/Composition"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"2e7ce03f-8b5f-4fdb-a261-e9dd451300ff"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9b5748b0-ad29-4b54-b557-2e53567754b0"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["6.1. Adding and deleting tensors", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"14ffc8ae-17ae-4076-8a7a-56b9edeb8612"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["TensorNetworkAdd",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/TensorNetworkAdd"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"6925580f-7b19-4b1d-8398-668b8b2ab621"],
 " attaches a new tensor to an existing network. Supply the network, the \
tensor, and the list of leg labels the tensor should be wired to. Any label \
that already exists in the network becomes a shared bond, contracting the new \
tensor with whatever already used it; labels that are new become additional \
free indices. The rank of the new tensor must match the length of its \
leg-label list, and shared labels must agree on dimension."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"54af3644-47af-4bee-b3ec-a0ddad6f2926"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

